      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "chore(codex): bump app-server to 0.144.0",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOpenClaw's managed Codex app-server is pinned to `0.143.0`. Models that require the current Codex client, including `gpt-5.6-sol`, reject that managed runtime with HTTP 400 and ask the user to upgrade Codex. Upgrading the system Codex CLI does not help because the plugin launches its separately managed package.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis bumps the managed `@openai/codex` package and minimum supported app-server version to `0.144.0`, refreshes the package locks and generated protocol schemas from the `rust-v0.144.0` Codex source, and updates the associated tests and documentation.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can run models requiring Codex `0.144.0` through the managed OpenClaw Codex harness without configuring an explicit `appServer.command` override.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Reproduced the HTTP 400 version rejection with OpenClaw's managed Codex runtime while the system Codex CLI was already `0.144.0`.\n- Confirmed that overriding `appServer.command` to the `0.144.0` binary removes the version rejection.\n- Refreshed the selected JSON schemas from the Codex `rust-v0.144.0` tag and validated every generated JSON file parses successfully.\n- `git diff --check` passes.\n- The full protocol export could not be rerun locally because the installed Rust compiler is `1.86.0`, while Codex `0.144.0` dependencies require up to Rust `1.91.0`.\n",
        "branch": "agent/bump-codex-app-server-0.144.0",
